# edges/dependencies.plan  --  math-linear-algebra Release 0.1
#
# Format: one "A B" edge per non-comment line. A is a NECESSARY PREREQUISITE
# for correctly stating, proving, interpreting, or applying B, within scope.
# Non-prerequisite relations (generalizes, equivalent_to, special_case_of,
# dual_of, contrasts_with, ...) live in edges/relations.tsv, NOT here.
#
# Roots (no incoming edges): the 16 cited bridge nodes in area `foundations`,
# plus `field` and the four notation_convention nodes.  See conventions.md.

# =============================================================================
# Foundations: what the cited roots are used for
# =============================================================================
# A field is a set with two operations; the vector space axioms quantify over
# its elements.
set field
set vector_space
# A linear map is a function first; linearity is a condition on a function.
function linear_map
# An isomorphism is a bijective linear map: bijectivity is the set-level notion.
bijection linear_isomorphism
# Row equivalence, similarity, and congruence are each verified to BE
# equivalence relations; the definition of one is needed to state that.
equivalence_relation row_equivalence
equivalence_relation similarity
equivalence_relation congruence
# V/U is a quotient set carrying induced operations; well-definedness on classes
# is the cited machinery.
quotient_set quotient_space
# "Finitely generated" means a spanning set that is a finite set.
finite_set finite_dimensional
# span, independence, and bases are stated over families indexed by an index set,
# which may be infinite even when only finite subsums are taken.
indexed_family linear_combination
indexed_family linear_independence
# Zorn on the poset of independent subsets ordered by inclusion is the proof;
# AC is what the statement is equivalent to.
zorns_lemma basis_existence_general
axiom_of_choice basis_existence_general
# Steinitz is an induction on the length of the independent list; dimension
# well-definedness and the Cholesky construction are likewise inductive.
induction_principle steinitz_exchange
induction_principle dimension_well_defined
induction_principle cholesky_factorisation
induction_principle gram_schmidt
# An inner product is real- or complex-valued and positive-definiteness needs
# the order on R.
real_number inner_product
real_number ordered_field_hyp
# The conjugate transpose needs complex conjugation; C is the algebraically
# closed field the capsule actually uses.
complex_number conjugate_transpose
complex_number fundamental_theorem_of_algebra
complex_number algebraically_closed_field
# FTA is what makes the C-specific triangularisation and normal spectral
# theorem available: it supplies the root the proofs peel off.
fundamental_theorem_of_algebra schur_triangularisation
fundamental_theorem_of_algebra spectral_theorem_normal
# The real spectral theorem's existence-of-an-eigenvector step maximises the
# Rayleigh quotient on the unit sphere: compactness gives a maximiser, EVT that
# it is attained.  (An algebraic route via C is recorded as a proof_route.)
compactness_cited spectral_theorem_symmetric
extreme_value_cited spectral_theorem_symmetric
# Characteristic and minimal polynomials are elements of F[t]; degree and
# division with remainder are what make the minimal polynomial well-defined.
polynomial_ring characteristic_polynomial
polynomial_ring minimal_polynomial
polynomial_ring cayley_hamilton

